## Deploy procedure (production)

Production deploys are automated via Docker image builds.

### How it works

1. Developer merges PR to `main`
2. GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/build-appdaemon.yml`) builds a Docker image
3. Image is pushed to GHCR with semver tags from `VERSION` file (e.g., `0.1.0`, `0.1.0-abc1234`, `latest`)
4. Flux detects the new image tag and rolls the Kubernetes deployment

### What the Docker build does

- Installs runtime deps from `docker/requirements-prod.txt`
- Processes `apps-prod.yaml` → `apps.yaml` (strips `disable: true` and `debug_preserve_run_dirs`)
- Stages app code and providers in the image
- At runtime, entrypoint copies code to `/conf/apps/` (writable emptyDir)

### What is NOT in the image

- `appdaemon.yaml` and `secrets.yaml` — come from Kubernetes Secret mounts
- Test files, dev configs, `.venv`, `__pycache__` — excluded by `.dockerignore`

### After merge

- Verify GitHub Actions build succeeded
- Check Flux reconciliation and pod status
- Verify at https://appdaemon.haynesops.com/ and check logs

### Scope communication

When you edit `appdaemon/**`:

- **Repo Updated** — changes are in the repo; will deploy automatically when merged to `main` via Docker image build

